---
description: How to verify and record a bug finding in BUGS.md during the FP-300 audit
alwaysApply: false
---

- Treat `HANDOVER.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, postmortems, meeting notes and
  name-tagged comments as claims to check, not facts. Several "done" items
  were false.
- Before calling something a bug, reproduce it: a failing test, a SQL query
  against the seeded DB, or an HTTP call. If it does not reproduce, record
  it as "not a bug" with the evidence (see S-30) instead of fixing it.
- Fix with the smallest change. Prefer a new `*.new.test.ts` / `*_test.go`
  that fails before the fix and passes after.
- An existing test that asserts the buggy behaviour may be corrected; list
  it under "Tests changed" in `BUGS.md` with the reason.
- Entry format: `### <ID> · <Critical|High|Medium|Low> · <symptom>`, then
  Where / What / Why / Impact / Fix, the test that proves it, and the effect
  on existing data (backfill, migration, or "none").
- Update the Status table and the Verification counts when you add entries.
